\label{prop:house}
There is an adelic constant $M_v=M(d, v)\geq 1$ with the following property. Let
$f(z)=z^d+a_{d-2}z^{d-2}+\cdots+a_0\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[z]$ be monic centered and
PCF. Then, for every place $v$ and every extension of $|\cdot|_v$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ we have that
\begin{enumerate}
\item\label{it:one} each $|a_i|_v\leq M_v$, and
\item\label{it:two} every critical point $c$ of $f$ and every $n, m\geq 0$, we have $|f^{n}(c)|_v\leq M_v$, and $|f^{n}(c)-f^m(c)|_v\leq M_v$.
\end{enumerate}

\label{lem:DZ}
Let $K$ be a number field, and let $M_v$ be an adelic constant. Then exists a linear form \begin{equation}\label{eq:loxtonform}L(x)=e_1x_1+\cdots +e_mx_m\in K[x]\end{equation} such that 
every $\alpha\inK^{\mathrm{cyc}}$ with $|\alpha|_w\leq M_v$ for all $v\in M_K$ and all places $w$ of $K(\alpha)$ above $v$ can be written as $\alpha=L(\zeta_1, ..., \zeta_m)$, with each $\zeta_i$ either zero or a root of unity.
